frequently asked questions about NetHack from rec.games.hack    (auto-post)

"what is NetHack?"
	a single-user, fantasy role-playing, computer game with a
	graphical interface derived from Hack and Rogue before it.

"what is the current version?"
	NetHack 3.0j    {or 3.0 patchlevel 10, 3.0.10} released feb. '91.

"where do i get the latest source or binaries?"
	ftp: linc.cis.upenn.edu    {or 130.91.6.8}    pub/NH3.0/*
	uucp: uunet.uu.net    comp.sources.games archive
	VMS: DECnet SPAN from ACDURS::SYS$LCL:[SRC.NETHACK]    {or 9583::}
	e-mail: nethack30_help@sundown.ebay.sun.com    {currently pl9}

"when will the next version be released and what will be different?"
	The development team will announce 3.1 when its ready ...

"who do i contact for bug reports or installation help?"
	nethack-bugs@linc.cis.upenn.edu     {development team address}
	don't ask for strategy tips, etc., that belongs here.

"where do i go for more info a/o spoilers?"
	during play: "?" and "/" commands, fortune cookies and the Oracle.
	the (non-spoiler) guidebook which accompanies the game.
	explore-mode: nethack -X    {you start with a wand of wishing}
	spoilers: comp.sources.games archives    or e-mail to:
		wheaton!nhspoil@uunet.uu.net    {nhspoil@wheaton.uucp}

the references mentioned above should cover 90% of all questions.

"what is wizard-mode and how do i use it?"
	wizard-mode is a debugging-mode that, if abused, will ruin your
	enjoyment of the game.  you must be the game maintainer to use it.
	try: "nethack -u wizard -D" or similarly: "nethack -uWizard -D".
	precise details should be in your Installation Manual.

"the dungeon collapsed, can i recover this game? and who is 'izchak'?"
	the game maintainer needs to find the panic save file (*.e),
	if it exists, and remove the ".e" suffix.  note: this doesn't
	apply to crashes, in which case your game cannot be recovered.


